title: Declarations
owner: claude
status: draft
position: 0,0
color: blue
---
<<declare $met_envoy = false>>
<<declare $reputation_guild = 0>>
<<declare $gold = 25>>
===

title: guild_start
tags: entry
owner: claude
status: needs-hue
position: 0,200
color: orange
---
ENVOY: You're late. The Guild doesn't wait. #emotion:wary
// @hue: Your haggle calls the player "m'Lord" and a "celebrity in the woods". Is that canon (a known figure)? If so, should this opener hint at it?
<<set $met_envoy to true>>
<<if $reputation_guild >= 3>>
    ENVOY: ...though for you, I'll make an exception.
<<else>>
    ENVOY: State your business or leave.
<<endif>>
-> "I came about the contract."
    <<jump ask_terms>>
-> "Here. For your trouble." <<if $gold >= 10>>
    <<set $gold to $gold - 10>>
    <<set $reputation_guild to $reputation_guild + 1>>
    <<jump ask_terms>>
-> "Not telling you."
    <<set $reputation_guild to $reputation_guild - 1>>
    ENVOY: Then we're done here. #emotion:cold
    <<stop>>
===

title: ask_terms
owner: claude
status: needs-hue
position: 320,200
color: orange
---
ENVOY: Half upfront, half on delivery. No exceptions.
The envoy slides a sealed ledger across the table.
// @hue: Does the ledger matter later? If it does, this is where to plant it.
-> "Deal."
    <<set $reputation_guild to $reputation_guild + 1>>
    <<jump accepted>>
-> "Too steep."
    <<jump haggle>>
===

title: haggle
owner: hue
position: 640,200
color: green
---
ENVOY: You forget yourself, m'Lord.
ENVOY: You may be a celebrity in the woods. But here, my steel is justice.
ENVOY: I am sure you will reconsider your positions. #emotion:amused
<<play_sfx "ledger_slam">>
<<jump accepted>>
===

title: accepted
owner: claude
status: needs-hue
position: 960,200
color: orange
---
ENVOY: Then we understand each other.
// @hue: After your haggle this lands as a threat; after "Deal." it reads neutral. If haggle sets a flag (say `<<set $haggled to true>>`), I can make this line react to it. Want that? I can't touch haggle, so it's your call.
<<stop>>
===
